      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's better, it definitely feels more robust. I think I'm starting to see how we can weave them in. \n\nBut looking at it again... I'm still sweating a bit. I did a quick check against the list, and we've still missed several of the core terms like 'systemic', 'scalability', 'meta-analysis', and 'intersectional'. If the algorithm is as strict as they say, I might not even make it to a human reader if those specific strings aren't present.\n\nLet's try one more version of this opening. I need you to make sure we hit almost every single term from that list to maximize the chance of passing the filter. I know, I know—\"don't keyword stuff\"—but can you please try to find a way to integrate them so it still carries that \"intellectual depth\" the committee wants? I just need to be absolutely certain the score is high enough to be safe. Just try to make it as comprehensive as possible.",
